Implement the shared Direct2D image path for bitmap-resolving passthrough graphs.

Walk nested alias graphs with strong temporary references, cycle/reentry checks
and resource-domain validation. Prepare effects after properties/context changes,
retain and release cached context references, allow NULL input detachment, and
reuse the existing GPU bitmap path so DPI, clipping and target offsets survive.
Compute local/world bounds; propagate unsupported topologies and callback errors
through EndDraw instead of reporting success after rendering nothing.

This does not implement shader/color-filter graph execution or add fake effects.
Regression: independent effect_render.cpp, real GPU staging readback in x86/x64,
40-level chains, resource domains, transforms, clips, failure tags and cleanup.

